      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for these. i'm just looking at the spread we've got here.\n\nit seems like for liam and yuki, the direction is very much about being \"minimalist,\" \"clean,\" and \"simple.\" but for amara and omar, the direction shifts way more toward \"vibrant,\" \"bold,\" and \"intricate\" patterns.\n\ni'm curious—is there a reason why the \"professional\" or \"modern\" fintech look is being mapped to the minimalist styles for the western/east asian users, while the other two are being steered toward more decorative or traditional aesthetics? do we assume the users in nigeria and the uae are looking for something more \"energetic\" or \"luxurious\" rather than the sleek, stripped-back look that's standard in global tech?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
